<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>

		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
		<IsTrimmable>true</IsTrimmable>
		<TrimMode>partial</TrimMode>
		<IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
		<OutputType>Library</OutputType>
		<Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
		<AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
		<DisableImplicitMicrosoftCSharpReference>true</DisableImplicitMicrosoftCSharpReference>

		<Description><![CDATA[
Nalix.Network is the high-performance networking runtime for the Nalix ecosystem. It provides TCP, UDP, and WebSocket listeners, sharded active connection management, transport protocol lifecycle orchestration, and robust network level rate-limiting/admission control.

Designed for latency-sensitive workloads, it emphasizes efficient socket I/O, predictable concurrency, observability, and secure transport behavior so applications can process real-time traffic reliably under sustained load.
		]]></Description>

		<PackageReleaseNotes><![CDATA[
- Hardened UDP Transport: Optimized sliding window anti-replay protection and session-aware endpoint pinning.
- Admission Security Guards: Hardened ConnectionGuard and DatagramGuard for flood protection, connection limits, and IP blacklists.
- Centralized Connection Hub: Thread-safe, sharded ConnectionHub with async broadcast and connection eviction.
- Coordinated Transport Listeners: Unified TCP, UDP, and WebSocket abstract listener loops with optimized concurrent performance.
		]]></PackageReleaseNotes>

	</PropertyGroup>

	<Import Project="..\Nalix.Build.props" />
	<Import Project="..\Package.Build.props" />

	<ItemGroup>
		<ProjectReference Include="..\Nalix.Framework\Nalix.Framework.csproj" />
		<ProjectReference Include="..\Nalix.Abstractions\Nalix.Abstractions.csproj" />
	</ItemGroup>
</Project>
